David Damerell wrote:
> Quoting   <david_ari_9@hotmail.com>:
>
>>YASD out of the blue. The cruelest was in Sokoban. I had a -2 AC (with
>>almost no metal) a bunch of spells, and had just received the amulet
>>of reflection... and then I went down the stairs, and got ambushed by
>>two centaurs. at melee range.
>
> Did you consider going back up the stairs?

I do that a LOT cycling into the mines early on.  Go down the stairs,
fight one or more monsters nearby, go back up the stairs.  While I heal
they also heal but they also don't move.  If I can kill even one monster
during a cycle eventually I'm clear. The idea would be to recognize the
danger first cycle then starting the second cycle pick one specific
centaur and attack it a few turns trying to kill it then cycle back up
stairs.  It's hard to get the timing right.

This situation shows why it matters to have as good a melee weapon as
possible even if you don't use it most of the time.  In a case like this
wielding Stormy makes the difference between eventually taking out both
centaurs and never eventually dying by missed timing.  Even an elven
broadsword will work better than a wielded dagger.  Except the special
effects of Magicbane.


